  "content": {
    "id": "p14-q5-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "5",
    "prompt": "Find all natural numbers less than 60 that are the product of three prime numbers.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$8,12,18,20,27,28,30,42,44,45,50,52$.\n\nInclude repeated primes and count exactly three prime factors.",
      "worked": "Write each product as $pqr$, where $p\\le q\\le r$ are primes. Repeated primes are allowed. Since $5^3>60$, the smallest prime factor is either $2$ or $3$.\n\nFor $p=2$, the condition $2q^2<60$ gives $q=2,3$ or $5$. The possible products are:\n$$\\begin{aligned}2\\times2\\times r&=8,12,20,28,44,52 &&(r=2,3,5,7,11,13),\\\\2\\times3\\times r&=18,30,42 &&(r=3,5,7),\\\\2\\times5\\times r&=50 &&(r=5).\\end{aligned}$$\nFor $p=3$, the condition $3q^2<60$ gives $q=3$. Thus\n$$3\\times3\\times r=27,45\\qquad(r=3,5).$$\nTherefore, in increasing order, the numbers are $8,12,18,20,27,28,30,42,44,45,50,52$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 84
  },
